$$\begin{aligned}16+t&=24\\t&=8\end{aligned}$$"}},{"id":"p9-guided-conclusion","type":"part","label":"4","prompt":"Answer in words: [[Nikki is 16 and Travis is 8 years old.|72]]","answer":{"short":"Nikki is 16 and Travis is 8 years old.","worked":"Nikki is 16 and Travis is 8 years old."}}]},"exerciseNumber":2}]},{"title":"Applications of simultaneous equations","blocks":[{"id":"p10-rectangle-block","type":"question","role":"guided-practice","heading":"Guided practice","skill":"simultaneous-word-problems","difficulty":"Development","content":{"id":"p10-rectangle-root","type":"group","label":"","prompt":"The perimeter of a rectangle is 56 cm. If the length of the rectangle is three times its breadth, determine the dimensions by setting up and solving two simultaneous equations.","children":[{"id":"p10-rectangle-step1","type":"part","label":"1","prompt":"","answer":{"short":"Let $l$ be the length and $b$ be the breadth, both in centimetres.","worked":"Let $l$ be the length and $b$ be the breadth, both in centimetres."}},{"id":"p10-rectangle-step2","type":"part","label":"2","prompt":"","answer":{"short":"$2l+2b=56$ (1); $l=3b$ (2).","worked":"$$\begin{align*}2l+2b&=56\qquad (1)\\l&=3b\qquad (2)\end{align*}$$"}},{"id":"p10-rectangle-step3","type":"part","label":"3","prompt":"","answer":{"short":"$b=7$, $l=21$.","worked":"Substitute (2) into (1).
