$$\begin{align*}2a-2c&=10\qquad (3)\end{align*}$$
Add (2) and (3).
$$\begin{align*}4a&=80\\a&=20\end{align*}$$
Substitute $a=20$ into (1).
$$\begin{align*}20-c&=5\\c&=15\end{align*}$$"}},{"id":"p10-tickets-step4","type":"part","label":"4","prompt":"","answer":{"short":"Child: $\$15$; adult: $\$20$.","worked":"Each child ticket costs $\$15$ and each adult ticket costs $\$20$."}}]},"exerciseNumber":2}]},{"title":"Applications of simultaneous equations","blocks":[{"id":"p11-guided-practice-block","type":"question","role":"guided-practice","heading":"Guided Practice","content":{"id":"p11-guided-practice-root","type":"group","label":"","prompt":"","children":[{"id":"p11-q1-node","type":"question","label":"","prompt":"John buys three daffodils and five petunias from the nursery and pays \$25.

Julia buys four daffodils and three petunias for \$26.

Determine the cost of each type of flower.","answer":{"short":"Petunias: $\$2$ each; daffodils: $\$5$ each.","worked":"Let $d$ be the cost of one daffodil in dollars and $p$ be the cost of one petunia in dollars.
$$\begin{align*}3d+5p&=25 &&(1)\\4d+3p&=26 &&(2)\end{align*}$$
Multiply (1) by 4 and (2) by 3:
$$\begin{align*}12d+20p&=100 &&(3)\\12d+9p&=78 &&(4)\end{align*}$$
Subtract (4) from (3):
$$\begin{align*}11p&=22\\p&=2\end{align*}$$
Substitute $p=2$ into (1):
$$\begin{align*}3d+5(2)&=25\\3d&=15\\d&=5\end{align*}$$
Each petunia costs $\$2$ and each daffodil costs $\$5$."}},{"id":"p11-q2-node","type":"question","label":"","prompt":"Alex buys 4 bolts and 6 washers for \$2.20 and Holly spends \$1.80 on 3 bolts and 5 washers at the same local hardware store. Determine the costs of each bolt and each washer.","answer":{"short":"Bolt: $\$0.10$; washer: $\$0.30$.","worked":"Let $b$ be the cost of one bolt in dollars and $w$ be the cost of one washer in dollars.
$$\begin{align*}4b+6w&=2.20 &&(1)\\3b+5w&=1.80 &&(2)\end{align*}$$
Multiply (1) by 3 and (2) by 4:
$$\begin{align*}12b+18w&=6.60 &&(3)\\12b+20w&=7.20 &&(4)\end{align*}$$
Subtract (3) from (4):
$$\begin{align*}2w&=0.60\\w&=0.30\end{align*}$$
Substitute $w=0.30$ into (1):
$$\begin{align*}4b+6(0.30)&=2.20\\4b&=0.40\\b&=0.10\end{align*}$$
Each bolt costs $\$0.10$ and each washer costs $\$0.30$."}},{"id":"p11-q3-node","type":"question","label":"","prompt":"A scientist mixes a 10% saline solution with a 30% saline solution to produce 200 mL of a 25% saline solution. Find the volume of each solution used.

